            <div xml:id="d371">

                <pb facs="0707" n="669" sameAs="frus:frus1919Parisv11/pg669"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">Paris Peace Conf. 184.13/130a: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Commission to Negotiate
                            Peace to the Secretary of
                    State</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Paris</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1919-11-19T11:00:00+00:00">November 19, 1919—11
                        a.m.</date></dateline></opener>
                <p>5285. From Polk. Many thanks for your 3801. Notified French we were leaving Paris
                    4th or 5th of December. Will you be kind enough to arrange with War Department
                    to have <hi rendition="#italic">America</hi> sail December 6th? I will probably
                    return on <hi rendition="#italic">America</hi>. We are already in touch with
                    General Connor arranging for shipping personnel and files. Am leaving for London
                    tomorrow and will be back Tuesday. Looking forward to seeing you soon. Polk.</p>
                <closer><hi rendition="#small-caps">Am</hi>[<hi rendition="#small-caps">erican</hi>]
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Mission</hi></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
